StructuralRule.Notes:
This rule should only report when the SharedPreferences$Editor object comes from unencrypted SharedPreference objects. For example:

    SharedPreferences pref1 = activity.getSharedPreferences(...);
    SharedPreferences.Editor editor1 = pref1.edit();
    editor1.putString("password", "123"); // unencrpted therefore vulnerable

    SharedPreferences pref2 = EncryptedSharedPreferences.create(...);
    SharedPreferences.Editor editor2 = pref2.edit();
    editor2.putString("password", "123"); // encrypted therefore not vulnerable

We can't distinguish the two SharedPreference objects by type because EncryptedSharedPreferences.create(...) returns the same android.content.SharedPreference type as other ways of retrieving SharedPreference objects. Dataflow rules such as a neutral flag source rule for EncryptedSharedPreferences.create() could be more accurate than this structural rule, but still aren't perfect because they don't work perfectly against fields (as seen in the customer test case of bug 66121). Since there isn't a perfect solution, I'm going with the simplest one - do not report anything if EncryptedSharedPreferences.create(...) is called anywhere in the enclosing class.

This has been split out from the password regex, which matches separately from properties

StructuralRule.Predicate:
FunctionCall call:
   call.function is [Function f:
       f.name matches "put.*"
       and f.enclosingClass.name == "android.content.SharedPreferences$Editor"
   ]
   and call.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*token$|^ssn.*|.*ssn$|.social.*security.*|.*encrypt(?!ed).*|plaintext|cleartext|.*creditcard.*|.*card(num|no).*|.*cvv.*|.*pin$"
   and not call.enclosingClass contains [Function anyFunc:
       anyFunc contains [FunctionCall:
           possibleTargets contains [Function:
               name == "create"
               and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class:
                   name == "androidx.security.crypto.EncryptedSharedPreferences"
               ]
           ]
       ]
   ]

FunctionCall call:
   call.function is [Function f:
       f.name matches "put.*"
       and f.enclosingClass.name == "android.content.SharedPreferences$Editor"
   ]
   and call.arguments[0].constantValue matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE"
   and not call.enclosingClass contains [Function anyFunc:
       anyFunc contains [FunctionCall:
           possibleTargets contains [Function:
               name == "create"
               and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class:
                   name == "androidx.security.crypto.EncryptedSharedPreferences"
               ]
           ]
       ]
   ]

FunctionCall call:
   call.function is [Function f:
       f.name matches "put.*"
       and f.enclosingClass.name == "android.content.SharedPreferences$Editor"
   ]
   and call.arguments[0].constantValue matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE"
   and not call.enclosingClass contains [Function anyFunc:
       anyFunc contains [FunctionCall:
           possibleTargets contains [Function:
               name == "create"
               and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class:
                   name == "androidx.security.crypto.EncryptedSharedPreferences"
               ]
           ]
       ]
   ]

